  "body": "### What is the issue with the HTML Standard?\n\nStep 2.1 of [8.1.6.6.2 HostEnqueueFinalizationRegistryCleanupJob(finalizationRegistry)](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/webappapis.html#hostenqueuefinalizationregistrycleanupjob) states:\n> Let entry be finalizationRegistry.[[CleanupCallback]].[[Callback]].[[Realm]]'s [environment settings object](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/webappapis.html#concept-realm-settings-object).\n\nHowever, [[Callback]] may not have a [[Realm]] slot. This is true for:\n- Bound functions\n- Proxied functions\n- Function.prototype (while not useful as a callback, it still technically doesn't have a [[Realm]] slot)\n\nThis should likely use the [GetFunctionRealm](https://tc39.es/ecma262/#sec-getfunctionrealm) abstract operation from the ecma262 specification.",
